WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.600
Welcome to Technical Solution. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Design and implement a solution that satisfies constraints and requirements.

2
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:20.880
Consider this scenario. A fast system cannot meet maintenance and support needs. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:30.860
Start with two steps: Assess technical options. Then Select justified design approaches. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:40.480
Continue with Develop the solution components. Then Confirm constraints are addressed. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:40.480 --> 00:01:00.770
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous design records, trade-off evidence, component tests tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: choosing an architecture before analyzing design trade-offs; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:15.020
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
